      ":question/math-academy-id": "e-3567",
      ":question/problem": "Is the function $y=f(x),$ plotted below, continuous at $x=0?$\n\n![](images/e3/e395863ca66a7e87fa335c56e5b6aeb1ec206893e57b155bf64e5ab07be7545c.png)",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Because there is an asymptote at $x=0,$ it is impossible to draw the function in the neighborhood of $x=0$ without taking our pencil off of the paper.\n\nTherefore, the function $y=f(x)$ is not continuous at $x=0.$"
