        ":question/id": "4ac549bb-41f9-5150-895e-d407a77f8e37",
        ":question/math-academy-id": "q-78131",
        ":question/problem": "![](images/3c/3c0dc4b8f7f45a5bc1177778431eccf9bcaac1bf6d520d605f9e6bc08d5b1d91.png)\n\nThe curve $y=f(x)$ is shown above. At which of the following points is $f(x)$ continuous?\n\nI. $x=-2$\n\nII. $x=0$\n\nIII. $x=2$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let's consider each point separately.\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is not continuous at $x=-2.$ Since there is an asymptote at $x=-2,$ it is impossible to draw the function in the neighborhood of $x=-2$ without taking our pencil off of the paper.\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=0.$ The graph can be drawn in the neighborhood of $x=0$ without taking our pencil off of the paper.\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=2.$ The graph can be drawn in the neighborhood of $x=2$ without taking our pencil off of the paper.\n\nHence, the correct answer is \"II and III only\"."
      },
